& [SupportDelta] distinguishes semantic readiness from physical desktop readiness
  + [complete] is exact query, trust, CLI, MCP, resident service, lifecycle, supervised model work, task-like contracts, faculty cycle, tool discovery, narrative continuity, and narrow workspace-effect governance
  + [formed_not_implemented] is multi-target SOP projections, general workflow programs, narrative activation, embodied effect broker, notifications, and learned task recognition
  + [absent] is desktop identity registry, observation and event adapters, capability and effect broker, trigger manager, task ledger, consent UI, undo contracts, fake-desktop fixture, and any real desktop authority

& [RequirementDelta] is COS-001 through COS-030
  + [application_delta] one user-facing Operator Shell coordinates task context, SOP retrieval, planning, tools, consent, effects, and reentry
  + [privacy_delta] foreground, subscribed, sensitive, local, and provider-projected context receive explicit identities and limits
  + [authority_delta] observation, preparation, reversible, persistent, external, and privileged effect classes require separate grants
  + [UX_delta] proposal cards, interruption budget, plan inspection, stop, undo, and explanation become tested contract surfaces
  + [proof_delta] deterministic fake desktop precedes any contained real effect

& [ReadinessDisposition] is application SJS after language-purpose reconciliation
  + [dependency] SMTC-SJS-01 defines stable SOP-T, SOP-W, SOP-I, exact, neural, and hybrid target boundaries
  + [next] COS-SJS-01 reconciles task state, context, privacy, triggers, capability, effects, memory, faculties, UX, recovery, and fixtures
  + [first_candidate_after_authority] is fake-desktop E0 and E1 proposal and preparation behavior only
  + [not_ready] is resident ambient monitoring, real desktop adapter, file mutation, application control, external communication, privileged operation, or autonomous routine
